{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.FluidDynamics.low_mode_block_uniformity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.low_mode_block_uniformity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.leray_bound_scaling","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.leray_bound_scaling","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L124-L142","doc":"**The vanishing-viscosity scaling of the Leray bound**: with the\nq-ladder viscosity `ν_q = ε/(2(1+ε))`, the discrete Leray bound\n`δ·ν_q·∑Ω ≤ E₀` of `low_mode_block_global` rearranges to\n`∑Ω ≤ 2(1+ε)·E₀/(δ·ε)` — the cumulative-enstrophy control\ndegrades at the explicit rate `ε⁻¹` because the in-QOU classical\nlimit sends the viscosity itself to zero.  (The fixed-`ν`\nmillennium formulation therefore sits across a substrate-to-\nphysical rescaling; flagged in the module docstring.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.tail_le_total","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.tail_le_total","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L113-L122","doc":"The trivial converse: the tail never exceeds the total (spectral\nenergies nonnegative), so unbounded tail forces unbounded total —\nthe reduction is an equivalence, not just an upper bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.uniformity_reduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.uniformity_reduction","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L99-L111","doc":"**The ε-uniformity reduction**: block enstrophy is at most\n`kB²·E + tail`.  Since `kB` and (via energy monotonicity,\n`low_mode_block_global.energy_le_initial`) `E ≤ E₀` are uniform in\nthe block width, an `ε`-uniform enstrophy bound holds **iff** the\nabove-band tail enstrophy is uniformly bounded.  The tail is the\nnamed open hypothesis — \"no enstrophy pile-up at the receding\nthreshold\"; nothing in the corpus proves or refutes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.banded_enstrophy_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.banded_enstrophy_le","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L76-L97","doc":"**The banded part is uniformly controlled by the energy**: if the\nladder is bounded by `kB` on the band (`n ≤ B`) and the spectral\nenergies are nonnegative, then the banded enstrophy is at most\n`kB²·E`.  This constant depends only on the *fixed* band, never on\nthe block width `m` — the `ε`-uniform half of the split. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.enstrophy_split","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.enstrophy_split","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L65-L74","doc":"**Enstrophy splits at any band**: block enstrophy = banded part +\ntail (a partition of the finite sum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.tailEnstrophy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.tailEnstrophy","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L59-L62","doc":"Above-band tail enstrophy: the part of the block enstrophy carried\nby rungs past the fixed band `B`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.blockEnstrophy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.blockEnstrophy","kind":"def","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L55-L57","doc":"Block enstrophy: the `k²`-weighted spectral energy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.blockEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.FluidDynamics.LowModeUniformity.blockEnergy","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/FluidDynamics/low_mode_block_uniformity.lean#L52-L53","doc":"Block energy: the total spectral energy over the block `range m`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}